{
  "hadith_number": 37,
  "text": "On the authority of the Son of Abbas, may Allah be pleased of them both, from the messenger of Allah, may the blessings and peace of Allah be upon him. It's that among the sayings he relates from his Lord, glorified and exalted be he, is that he said, Allah has written down the good deeds and the bad ones. Then he explained it by saying that he who has intended a good deed, but if he has intended it and has done it, Allah writes it down with himself, as from ten good deeds to 700 times, or many times over. But if he has intended a bad deed and has not done it, Allah writes it down with himself as a full good deed. But if he has intended it and has done it, Allah writes it down as one bad deed. It was related by Al-Bukhari and Muslim in their to Sahihin in these words.",
